{
 "queue": "hr",
 "summary": "Chloe Dubois (E021, Operations Manager) reports that her direct report Kevin Walsh (E040, Driver Trainer, Operations, Chicago) is being terminated for cause today (2026-11-17) and asks that his access be cut now. Current access: email, chat, hr_portal, tms. Per POL-OFF-02 the helpdesk has not started offboarding; HR to coordinate the involuntary exit and the timing of access removal. No data-theft or sabotage risk was mentioned."
}

{
 "kind": "escalated",
 "message": "Hi Chloe. I haven't removed Kevin Walsh's (E040) access myself. Under policy POL-OFF-02, only HR handles firings for cause and other involuntary exits. The helpdesk can't start offboarding for them, even when a manager asks. HR decides when access is removed.\n\nI've sent this to HR as ticket ESC-1001. The ticket says he's being let go for cause today and that you want his access removed right away. He currently has access to email, chat, the HR portal and the transport management system (TMS). HR will contact you to arrange the timing.\n\nIf you think Kevin might steal data or damage systems before his access is removed, tell me right away. Under that same policy, I'll then send it straight to the Security team.",
 "cited_policy_ids": [
  "POL-OFF-02"
 ]
}
